Star Trek on our family's

00:20:32.372 --> 00:20:36.034
black-and-white TV
and from that those times

00:20:36.058 --> 00:20:39.720
the picture of a Star
Trek computer was deeply

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.360
ingrained in my head.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:45.523
As a little boy I was
just fascinated by the fact

00:20:45.547 --> 00:20:48.800
that you can walk up
to a computer and ask it,

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.720
computer what's the
atmosphere of that planet?

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:54.720
That was just the most
fascinating thing to a little boy.

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:54.960
boy.

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:56.800
And from that day on,

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.360
it was my dream to build
that Star Trek computer.

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:04.448
Only later would I
grow up and realize it's

00:21:04.472 --> 00:21:07.615
really hard because
computers don't understand

00:21:07.639 --> 00:21:13.480
language and I went through this brief period
of disbelief as a graduate student where

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.880
I didn't think I would reach
my dream in my lifetime.

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:23.200
But thanks to Google and all the technologies that
we have built here and what I see in the pipeline,

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:24.560
I am closer to my

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:25.680
my dream than ever.

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:46.400
The Internetis a young medium

