00:26:42.680 --> 00:26:45.160
which was a kind of glint
in their eyes and a smile,

00:26:45.960 --> 00:26:49.397
and the sense that this was
just the beginning of something

00:26:49.421 --> 00:26:52.560
much bigger than even
you at this point can imagine.

00:26:58.640 --> 00:26:59.200
At Harvard,

00:26:59.200 --> 00:27:02.680
we only permitted Google to
digitize books in the public domain.

00:27:03.240 --> 00:27:06.968
But the other research
libraries that Google first went to

00:27:06.992 --> 00:27:10.720
permitted Google to digitize
books covered by copyright.

00:27:11.320 --> 00:27:14.000
As soon as you get
into the copyright area,

00:27:14.680 --> 00:27:17.000
things get rapidly complicated.

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:29.360
We're allowing Google
to scan all of our books,

00:27:30.120 --> 00:27:32.840
those in the public domain
and those still in copyright.

00:27:33.440 --> 00:27:35.240
We believe it is legal,

00:27:36.040 --> 00:27:36.440
ethical,

00:27:36.920 --> 00:27:40.360
and a noble endeavor that
will transform our society.

00:27:41.560 --> 00:27:41.800
Legal,

00:27:42.480 --> 00:27:45.048
because we believe
copyright law allows us fair use

00:27:45.072 --> 00:27:47.640
of the millions of books
that are being digitized.

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:01.423
Fair use is a piece of
American copyright law that

00:28:01.447 --> 00:28:05.360
allows us to make copies
without asking any permission,

00:28:05.520 --> 00:28:08.760
without paying any fee
for certain carved out uses.

00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:11.560
I happen to think Google's
fair use defense is strong.

00:28:12.120 --> 00:28:12.840
One of the things...

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:16.682
that courts have done
over the last decade or so

00:28:16.706 --> 00:28:20.388
is decided that search
engines who routinely make

00:28:20.412 --> 00:28:23.833
copies of information
are making fair uses when

00:28:23.857 --> 00:28:27.800
they do it in order to help
people find information.

00:28:27.840 --> 00:28:29.320
information that
they're looking for.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:32.508
One of the things Google
has done is provide

00:28:32.532 --> 00:28:35.040
links to places where
you can buy the book.

00:28:35.680 --> 00:28:36.320
They scanned,

00:28:36.360 --> 00:28:37.680
but they did not
release the copy.

00:28:38.080 --> 00:28:41.040
You could not search
except for keywords.

00:28:41.360 --> 00:28:43.480
You could not see a
page except for snippets.

00:28:44.360 --> 00:28:51.280
They were trying to allow indexing and
searching without allowing people to get copies.

00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:54.080
And we will protect all
copyrighted materials.

00:28:54.560 --> 00:28:56.480
your work in that archive,

00:28:57.240 --> 00:28:57.680
let me repeat.

00:28:57.680 --> 00:28:58.040
I repeat that.

00:28:58.920 --> 00:29:04.480
I guarantee you we will
protect all copyrighted materials.

00:29:05.720 --> 00:29:10.840
I assure you we understand that providing
public access to materials and copyright,

00:29:11.280 --> 00:29:12.920
particularly
those still in print,

00:29:13.440 --> 00:29:14.360
would be unlawful.

00:29:15.240 --> 00:29:19.868
One of the things that you need to
understand about Google is that they try

00:29:19.892 --> 00:29:24.520
to roll out projects first and then to
think about the consequences later.

00:29:25.200 --> 00:29:29.640
So you would often see them experiment
with something that looks very cool.

00:29:29.960 --> 00:29:32.160
It may be the Google
Street View project.

00:29:32.880 --> 00:29:35.400
Google launched
Street View in 2007,

00:29:35.680 --> 00:29:38.048
part of the search
engine's long-term goal to

00:29:38.072 --> 00:29:40.440
create a virtual 3D
map of the whole planet,

00:29:40.680 --> 00:29:41.840
right down to street level.

00:29:42.880 --> 00:29:45.808
But investigations have revealed
that Google's Street View cars

00:29:45.832 --> 00:29:48.760
were collecting more than just
photographs for their databanks.

00:29:49.920 --> 00:29:52.880
Their antennas were also
hoovering up personal information.

00:29:53.080 --> 00:29:54.800
from unencrypted Wi-Fi networks,

00:29:54.880 --> 00:29:57.280
including Internet
history and passwords.

00:29:59.160 --> 00:30:00.560
I think the case of...

00:30:00.800 --> 00:30:02.960
Google collecting
Wi-Fi information.

00:30:03.520 --> 00:30:07.840
It reveals a complete lack of respect
for privacy within the corporation.

00:30:08.040 --> 00:30:09.920
Such projects often reveal that

00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:14.280
Google does not fully understand the
social consequences of its own work.

00:30:27.640 --> 00:30:30.040
We actually do more
search queries in China alone.

